Third-party components vendored or referenced
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

As of the C99 migration phase, all C++ networking, cryptography, and serialization dependencies have been eradicated in favor of native POSIX/Windows kernel APIs and the determ::c99 cryptographic suite.

All core consensus, networking, and cryptographic primitives execute
under bare-metal C99 with zero dynamic third-party library dependencies.

